     You can get aggravate monsters as an intrinsic by eating a human
(this also decreases your luck to -10, really messing up any relations
you previously had with your God, unless you can get that back up to par
before praying the next time.  Takes, what, about 2000 turns?).   Luck
is a hidden attribute on a scale of -10 to 10 and affects everything
from your wishing success ("Unfortunately, nothing happens" have been
the last words of many computer terminals that had the bad luck to have
been played by a hacker who zapped a wand of wishing with low luck.)
     You can also get if from eating a dead cat or dog.  Not a jackal or
a tiger, just the "little/large dog" and "dog", and the equivilant for
cats (kitten/housecat/large cat).  Doesn't matter if it was your pet.
     Aggravate monsters makes some peaceful monsters hostile.  I *wish*
it were all of them; I *hate* friendly monsters.  They slow down my game
horrendously unless I have a pet to kill them off (and sometimes they
even kill off my pet themselves).  The only case I can think of where a
monster being friendly actually helps me is in the case of the golden
naga, which is a very difficult monster to fight without magic
resistance.
     I have a question regarding aggravate monster: does it counteract
stealth by alerting monsters to your presence?  This would be bad.  Or
does it just piss some of them off?

